## Proof

**Setup.** The number-8 graph $G$ has one vertex $v$ (of degree 4) and two loop edges, so $G \cong \bigvee_2 S^1$ (a bouquet of 2 circles) with first Betti number $b_1(G) = 2$.

**Farber's theorem (bounds).** For any path-connected space $X$, Farber established:
$$\operatorname{zerodivcup}(X) + 1 \;\leq\; \operatorname{TC}(X) \;\leq\; 2\dim(X) + 1,$$
where $\operatorname{zerodivcup}(X)$ is the zero-divisor cup length (the maximum number of positive-degree zero-divisors of the diagonal $\Delta: X \hookrightarrow X \times X$ whose cup product is nonzero) and $\dim$ is the covering dimension.

